      "description": "Tiny, brilliantly-coloured birds endemic to the Caribbean islands, with vivid green upperparts, a red throat, and a long, flattened bill adapted for sallying after insects. Todies are the closest New World relatives of the kingfishers and motmots. Despite their diminutive size, they have loud, buzzing calls and are feisty defenders of their territories.",
